{
  "dom_id": "step-q342862",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=3{x}^{3}-8x.$\n\n$\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=$ \n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{3}-8x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-8 \\\\  & =9{x}^{2}-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{x}^{2}-8) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 9x \\\\  & =18x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
